        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "### Instructor for PHP sales guidance\n\n- **Mindset:** Be a curious challenger. Share a useful insight about the cost of unreliable LLM outputs, connect it to the prospect’s actual workflow, and guide the discussion toward a measurable next step.\n- **Discovery and demo:** Ask for a real malformed LLM response, trace the manual rework or other impact it caused, then demonstrate how Instructor for PHP handles that specific case with structured validation and retry feedback.\n- **Avoid:** Generic demos, assuming validation is the prospect’s main pain, or implying retries solve every failure. Verify the library handles the prospect’s case before pitching, and quantify the impact where possible.\n- **Example next step:** Offer to test a real support-summary response and measure whether validation and retries reduce cleanup work.\n\n### Product reference\n\nInstructor for PHP is a framework-agnostic PHP library for extracting validated, structured data from LLM outputs. It supports text, chat, and image inputs; class-based or dynamic schemas; validation and retries; streaming, embeddings, context caching, and observability. Its unified API works with providers including OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Cohere, Groq, Mistral, and Ollama. Typical setup uses Composer, a PHP response class, and `StructuredOutput`; Symfony validation and customization are also supported. Example use cases include document processing, support automation, and analysis.",
